  "operative_text": "Section 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-306(a)): Subject to subsection (c) of this section, the Secretary shall issue a permit within a reasonable time to a person who the Secretary finds:\nSection 1 (Md. Code Ann., Public Safety § 5-306(a)(6)): based on an investigation: (i) has not exhibited a propensity for violence or instability that may reasonably render the person’s possession of a handgun a danger to the person or to another; and (ii) has good and substantial reason to wear, carry, or transport a handgun, such as SELF–DEFENSE OR a finding that the permit is necessary as a reasonable precaution against apprehended danger."
